WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.440
“The immigration crisis in europe…”
“…Three children drowned…”

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.259
“…Syrian refugees…”
“…it’s become a symbol of desperation…”

00:00:06.259 --> 00:00:10.559
“…a surge of refugees…”
“…Among the dead, several children, including

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.200
a baby girl.”

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:12.740
Sen. Dick Durbin (D-IL): “One issue that
needs to be addressed is the overly broad

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:20.080
prohibition in our immigration law that excludes
any refugee who has provided any kind of support

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:25.429
to an army rebel group. Even a group that
we in the United States support.”

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:33.200
Rep. Michael McCaul (R-TX): “This would
be a federally sanctioned welcome party, if

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:36.219
you will, to potential terrorists in the United
States.”

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.600
Sam Stein, Huffington Post: Could we take
more? I mean Germany is taking 800,000…

00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:41.920
John Kerry: Well i’m not talking about taking
more on a permanent basis.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:48.109
Josh Earnest: It warrants mentioning has provided
more than 4 billion dollars in humanitarian assistance.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.819
But no thinking of bringing more Syrian refugees
to the US?

00:01:52.819 --> 00:01:54.630
Earnest: At this point, I don’t have any
announcement along those lines.

